 {
  "query_id": "S08",
  "question": "How is the probability of getting at least one four in three rolls of a die calculated?",
  "answerable": true,
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "The probability of getting at least one four in three rolls of a die can be calculated by first finding the probability of not observing a four on any of the rolls and then subtracting this probability from 1. The probability of not observing a four on a single roll is \\( \\frac{5}{6} \\). Therefore, the probability of not observing a four in three rolls is \\( \\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)^3 \\). The probability of getting at least one four in three rolls is then \\( 1 - \\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)^3 \\).\n\n[ B:openstax-pds:p135:1 ]",
